title: 'pallet-broker: fix double counting of provisionally pooled regions'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    A provisionally pooled region could be counted twice in the instantaneous pool after it was
    re-pooled, assigned, partitioned or interlaced, because its contribution was not found under
    the region id.

    `ContributionRecord` now stores `claimed_until` and `end` instead of `length`, and the
    contribution keeps its key for its whole lifetime. Claiming revenue no longer moves it, so
    `RevenueClaimPaid::next` is always the claimed region id, or `None` once fully claimed.
    Tooling which read the claim progress from `next.begin` should read `claimed_until` from
    `InstaPoolContribution` instead. Unpooling cuts `end` to the current timeslice, so revenue
    for the timeslices that already passed stays claimable.

    Runtimes must run `pallet_broker::migration::MigrateV5ToV6`.
crates:
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: major
- name: coretime-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
